# Vercel's CLI uploads the working directory, and `backend/.env` is read by
# backend/config.py's SettingsConfigDict(env_file=...). Without this, a local
# dev .env ships to production and supplies every value the platform does not
# override - which is how a preview deployment came up announcing
# `http://localhost:3000` as an allowed CORS origin.
.env
.env.*
*.env
backend/.env
backend/.env.*

# Not needed at runtime, and they are most of the bundle.
.git
.github
docs
frontend
backend/tests
# backend/alembic is deliberately NOT excluded: #36 runs migrations as a
# deploy step, and .vercelignore drops files from the upload entirely, so
# excluding them would leave the build with nothing to migrate from.
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/node_modules
.vercel/output

# Local tooling and leftovers.
.claude
.vscode
.logs
*.deb
Makefile
